20 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a cloud-edge-device architecture. The cloud layer includes control and compute nodes. The edge layer comprises nodes with EdgeCore, hosting containers within pods. EdgeX Foundry connects to various devices like sensors, cameras, and agricultural IoT devices.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing a cloud computing architecture. At the top, a green cloud labeled \215Cloud center\216 connects to two server towers representing \215Edge nodes.\216 Below, a tablet with gears symbolizes \215End devices.\216 Arrows indicate data flow between components.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a cloud-edge network. A cloud center at the top connects to two sets of edge nodes, labeled Edge nodes 1 and Edge nodes 2. Each set of edge nodes connects to multiple end devices, represented by blue tablets with gear icons, labeled as End devices 1. Arrows indicate data flow between the cloud, edge nodes, and end devices.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a hierarchical network structure. At the bottom are end devices represented by a tablet with gears. They connect upward to Edge Nodes 1, depicted as two server towers. Above are Edge Nodes 2, another set of server towers. At the top is a cloud labeled \215Cloud center,\216 indicating the flow of data from end devices to the cloud center through the edge nodes.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a hydroponic greenhouse system using LoRa technology. Various sensors, including ultrasonic, LEDs, fans, LLC 3779, and DHT11, connect to a gateway. Data is processed through edge computing with Node-RED, MQTT, and PID controllers, integrating with satellite communication. The Internet facilitates remote monitoring via a dashboard showing temperature, humidity, water levels, and smart lighting controls. A separate inset displays a hydroponic setup with plants.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 70 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a smart agriculture monitoring system using LoRaWAN and 5G. It involves temperature, humidity, light, and wind monitoring, connected to edge computing gateways. These gateways link to a central cloud via 5G for soil moisture, irrigation, and pest monitoring.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 71 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a network architecture for a smart strawberry greenhouse system. It includes global and edge networks, sensor motes, actuators, and a water tank. Icons represent components like a global cloud, watering valve, and backhaul connection. Sensors gather data, enabling the control of actuators in the greenhouse, optimizing water usage through wireless communication.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 72 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a high-frequency monitoring and service system for agriculture. It shows satellite data aggregation leading to management and production subsystems, including guidance and scheduling apps. This system provides macro-management, service, field information, and operation scheduling, facilitated by intelligent computing models and precise control via agricultural machinery and drones.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 51 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 73 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a layered technology system with six layers: Physical layer with sensors, Data collection with a gateway, Data storage with processing, Communication with IoT gateway, Cloud storage with information, and Virtual layer for simulations. Features a feedback system connecting the layers.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 52 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 74 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the integration of animal farming with environment and technology. At the center, animals are monitored for environmental effects like CO2, NH3, and temperature. Farming strategies include feeding, water supply, and grooming. Facility environment involves Internet of Things for fine control. Intelligent perception employs sensors for data collection.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 53 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
30 0 obj
<< /A 75 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a layered architecture of a distributed edge computing network. The top layer shows a virtual distributed edge computing network with an edge computing supervisor managing virtual objects, connectivity, task management, monitoring, and database. Below, the physical distributed edge computing network displays three Raspberry Pi devices labeled as Edge Gateways 1, 2, and 3. The bottom layer represents the physical distributed Internet of Things devices network with Raspberry Pi devices handling HTTP humidity and IoTivity temperature, connected to a Smart Home Emulator that produces smart home environment parameters. Arrows indicate communication interfaces.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 57 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
31 0 obj
<< /A 76 0 R /Alt (Flowchart of a hierarchical network model with three tiers: Cloud, Network, and Fog. The Cloud Tier includes data servers for uploading data and aggregating parameters. The Network Tier features a WAN network with routers and switches. The Fog Tier has participants sending local models to servers. Below is the Edge Tier showing various industrial and urban environments. Arrows indicate data flow, with icons representing data upload/download, real/adversarial samples, and global/local models. A legend explains symbols used in the diagram.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 59 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
32 0 obj
<< /A 77 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a farming management system integrated with cloud, fog, and edge computing. The cloud provides disease identification, routing, weather, and growth estimation services. A static fog zone handles resource scheduling and digital twin operations, while a mobile fog zone involves drones and tractors. The edge layer includes sensors for environmental data. A farmer interacts with the system through a GUI, and satellite data complements the setup.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 60 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
